483
00:36:44,121 --> 00:36:46,748
Pocket money . Keep your lady happy .

484
00:36:46,915 --> 00:36:48,584
Well , what can I do you for ?

485
00:36:48,750 --> 00:36:50,586
You heard about the missing kid ?

486
00:36:50,752 --> 00:36:52,504
A parent 's worst fear .

487
00:36:52,671 --> 00:36:57,467
Well , while we were up at the Marsten house making that delivery

488
00:36:57,634 --> 00:37:00,095
I looked in the back of the new owner 's car .

489
00:37:00,762 --> 00:37:03,432
I saw a plastic bag in the back seat .

490
00:37:03,974 --> 00:37:05,434
It was leaking .

491
00:37:07,519 --> 00:37:09,521
Was it little-boy-sized ?

492
00:37:10,814 --> 00:37:12,107
It was head-sized .

493
00:37:14,026 --> 00:37:16,445
The new owner is Richard Straker .

494
00:37:16,612 --> 00:37:20,073
You think he killed the missing Glick boy and kept the head ?

495
00:37:20,240 --> 00:37:21,491
I 'm not saying all that .

496
00:37:21,658 --> 00:37:23,952
What will that do to his antique business ?

497
00:37:24,369 --> 00:37:28,624
- lt was leaking all over the leather seats . - Did you tell Mike what you saw ?

498
00:37:28,832 --> 00:37:32,127
No. I didn 't think much of it at the time , until today .

499
00:37:34,171 --> 00:37:37,966
So why tell me ? Go tell Parkins Gillespie , if you think it 's important .

500
00:37:38,133 --> 00:37:40,093
I 'm telling you because you know him .

501
00:37:40,302 --> 00:37:41,512
Relax , Floyd .

502
00:37:41,678 --> 00:37:46,975
Straker called me this morning , excited about tackle and shacks .

503
00:37:47,142 --> 00:37:50,729
Seems he tried his hand at ice fishing and finds it relaxing .

504
00:37:51,355 --> 00:37:52,814
Ice fishing .

505
00:37:53,649 --> 00:37:58,737
Maybe he bagged a tuna or cod , whatever you swamp Yankees pull out of these lakes .

506
00:37:59,780 --> 00:38:01,406
Ice fishing .

507
00:38:02,199 --> 00:38:03,992
Well , that 's a relief .

508
00:38:05,994 --> 00:38:08,163
I was driving myself crazy .

509
00:38:08,330 --> 00:38:09,915
I understand

510
00:38:10,082 --> 00:38:12,835
but we have to be careful , Floyd .

511
00:38:13,001 --> 00:38:15,921
Loose talk can ruin people .

512
00:38:16,088 --> 00:38:20,425
My first suspect was the other new guy in town . Some hotshot writer .

513
00:38:20,592 --> 00:38:22,678
- What writer ? - Mears .

514
00:38:22,845 --> 00:38:26,348
Nice enough , but a city guy . A bit abrasive . You know him ?

515
00:38:27,808 --> 00:38:29,810
Ben Mears .

516
00:38:31,854 --> 00:38:33,480
I know of him .

517
00:38:34,398 --> 00:38:35,774
I better get back to work .

518
00:38:35,941 --> 00:38:37,985
Hey , thanks for last night .

519
00:38:38,193 --> 00:38:40,737
And thanks for coming to me first on this .

520
00:38:40,904 --> 00:38:42,531
Bishop 's Lake .

521
00:38:43,740 --> 00:38:45,868
That 's the best spot for ice fishing .

522
00:38:46,994 --> 00:38:48,787
I 'll tell Straker .

523
00:38:48,954 --> 00:38:51,373
You 're on my short list , buddy .

524
00:39:23,238 --> 00:39:24,448
Dud .

525
00:39:25,032 --> 00:39:27,326
I 'm sorry , Dud . I can 't use you today .

526
00:39:28,076 --> 00:39:29,953
What ? Why not ?

527
00:39:31,079 --> 00:39:35,000
Ruth Crockett . You shouldn 't have been messing with her , Dud .

528
00:39:35,167 --> 00:39:38,212
Now Larry 's threatened to pull all the accounts .

529
00:39:38,378 --> 00:39:42,799
Well , I can 't put you on the truck , Dud . I can 't afford it .

530
00:39:44,259 --> 00:39:47,721
But we 're friends , Mike . We 're best friends .

531
00:39:47,930 --> 00:39:49,389
I know. I know .

532
00:39:49,598 --> 00:39:51,308
We still are .

533
00:39:52,518 --> 00:39:53,936
What will I do ?

534
00:39:56,647 --> 00:39:58,190
I don 't know .

535
00:39:58,607 --> 00:40:01,777
You know , I 'll help you find another job .

536
00:40:02,486 --> 00:40:04,696
Until then , look , just take this

537
00:40:05,322 --> 00:40:07,074
to hold you over , all right .

538
00:40:10,494 --> 00:40:12,579
It 's not your fault , Dud .

539
00:40:13,330 --> 00:40:17,000
Whatever you did , it was just , you know , misunderstood .

540
00:40:17,543 --> 00:40:18,877
I 'm sorry .

541
00:40:23,507 --> 00:40:25,300
Danny , can you hear me ?

542
00:40:26,093 --> 00:40:27,803
Danny ? Can you hear me ?

543
00:40:28,011 --> 00:40:30,305
If you can hear me , blink your eyes .

544
00:40:34,351 --> 00:40:36,144
He 's in acute mental shock .

545
00:40:36,520 --> 00:40:39,314
Maybe from excessive fear , grief

546
00:40:39,815 --> 00:40:42,401
or some sort of emotional trauma .

547
00:40:43,193 --> 00:40:44,403
Excuse me .

548
00:40:46,864 --> 00:40:48,365
He 's getting worse .

549
00:40:50,909 --> 00:40:52,202
Marjorie .

550
00:40:55,455 --> 00:40:57,165
I believe this is Danny 's .

551
00:41:04,381 --> 00:41:07,050
- Yes , doctor . - Doctor .

552
00:41:08,594 --> 00:41:12,097
Sometimes the power of prayer and local facilities have limits .

553
00:41:12,264 --> 00:41:15,726
It 's shock , Father . Your car didn 't hit him .

554
00:41:17,186 --> 00:41:18,645
He 'll snap out of it .

555
00:41:26,695 --> 00:41:28,030
Stop it .

556
00:41:33,327 --> 00:41:35,495
Hi . How 's little Roy today ?

557
00:41:35,662 --> 00:41:38,707
He 's fine , Jimmy . See for yourself .

558
00:41:43,045 --> 00:41:46,256
Hello . Hi . How you doing ?

559
00:41:46,423 --> 00:41:48,926
I really appreciate your help , Jimmy .

560
00:41:49,092 --> 00:41:52,721
Maybe after you finish with Roy , I could buy you lunch .

561
00:41:52,888 --> 00:41:56,600
You know , I usually have my lunch in the cafeteria , Sandy .

562
00:41:56,767 --> 00:41:58,852
Well , little Roy and I could join you .

563
00:41:59,645 --> 00:42:01,563
That wouldn 't be a good idea .

564
00:42:02,940 --> 00:42:06,652
- What would your husband say ? - " Order a salad . Your ass is fat . "

565
00:42:09,238 --> 00:42:10,405
That was a joke .

566
00:42:11,448 --> 00:42:14,743
Most doctors love kids . They have pictures all over the office .

567
00:42:15,452 --> 00:42:17,371
It helps the patient relax .

568
00:42:17,538 --> 00:42:21,750
They figure , " This doctor 's so busy thinking about his kids

569
00:42:21,917 --> 00:42:24,378
he 's not thinking about my naked body . "

570
00:42:25,462 --> 00:42:29,299
Yeah , well , I love kids , you know . They 're great to work with .

571
00:42:29,466 --> 00:42:31,885
They have this , you know

572
00:42:32,052 --> 00:42:35,264
way to thank you with their eyes .

573
00:42:35,430 --> 00:42:39,101
Yeah , but you love your toys too . I mean , look at this car .

574
00:42:39,268 --> 00:42:40,602
- Still a player . - Player ?

575
00:42:40,811 --> 00:42:44,231
- You think this car 's too dope for Doctor C. ? - Maybe .

576
00:42:50,779 --> 00:42:54,449
I only said " player " because I know how you were at Dell 's .

577
00:42:54,616 --> 00:42:58,412
- l danced with you , remember ? - Oh , yeah. I remember .

578
00:42:59,830 --> 00:43:02,583
Would you pull over ? I have to check on little Roy .

579
00:43:02,749 --> 00:43:04,084
Sure .

580
00:43:23,187 --> 00:43:24,646
I can 't .

581
00:43:31,862 --> 00:43:33,947
You 're still a nice guy .

582
00:43:34,114 --> 00:43:35,699
You are .

583
00:43:36,533 --> 00:43:39,328
If I could have chose everything in my life

584
00:43:39,953 --> 00:43:42,039
I 'd have chose a man like you .

585
00:44:42,850 --> 00:44:46,562
The more interesting items are in the store .

586
00:44:46,770 --> 00:44:49,731
I 'm sorry. I was looking for a local boy who 's missing .

587
00:44:49,898 --> 00:44:52,067
I don 't think you 'll find him here .

588
00:44:52,317 --> 00:44:54,069
No .

589
00:44:56,280 --> 00:44:59,074
I 'm Ben Mears , Mr. Straker . Been anxious to meet you .

590
00:44:59,241 --> 00:45:00,617
Richard .

591
00:45:00,784 --> 00:45:03,912
You and your partner took the house I was interested in .

592
00:45:04,538 --> 00:45:06,123
You comfortable up there ?

593
00:45:07,124 --> 00:45:11,128
Well , it 's a handful , Ben .

594
00:45:13,964 --> 00:45:16,133
I hope you find the little boy .

595
00:45:16,300 --> 00:45:20,137
Somehow , I don 't think we will . Not alive , anyway .

596
00:45:20,304 --> 00:45:21,763
How 's your alibi ?

597
00:45:23,515 --> 00:45:25,100
Excuse me ?

598
00:45:25,976 --> 00:45:29,354
The police spoke with me today . We 're both new in town .

599
00:45:29,521 --> 00:45:34,109
We 're not even new. ln a small town like this , we 're strangers the first 20 years .

600
00:45:34,776 --> 00:45:37,446
Well , I happen to like it here , Ben .

601
00:45:38,197 --> 00:45:39,698
And your partner ?

602
00:45:39,865 --> 00:45:41,408
- Mr . Barlow ? - You a reporter ?

603
00:45:41,575 --> 00:45:43,035
Writer .

604
00:45:43,202 --> 00:45:46,079
- Critics call me " typist . " - " Typist " ?

605
00:45:46,955 --> 00:45:48,248
Typist .

606
00:45:49,166 --> 00:45:51,793
Well , if you 're curious about the house ...

607
00:45:55,005 --> 00:45:56,798
The truth is the place scares me .

608
00:45:57,007 --> 00:46:00,969
Well , then you never intended to take it , did you , Mr. Typist ?

609
00:46:11,522 --> 00:46:13,190
- lt 's Romeo . - More like Hannibal .

610
00:46:13,357 --> 00:46:14,608
Ruth !

611
00:46:17,152 --> 00:46:19,321
- Can I talk to you ? - Send him for pizza .

612
00:46:19,530 --> 00:46:21,990
- Hey , go wash my car ! - Shut up .

613
00:46:23,825 --> 00:46:26,203
I got fired , Ruth .

614
00:46:26,787 --> 00:46:29,998
Mike said I shouldn 't have been messing with you .

615
00:46:31,625 --> 00:46:36,338
I was thinking maybe you could talk to your father so I can get my job back .

616
00:46:36,547 --> 00:46:40,175
It wouldn 't do any good . He 's mega-protective .

617
00:46:40,384 --> 00:46:43,387
- l hate my father more than you do . - Really ?

618
00:46:43,554 --> 00:46:47,266
Well , I still like you , Ruth . I really do .

619
00:46:48,475 --> 00:46:50,435
You seem like a nice person , Dud .

620
00:46:50,602 --> 00:46:53,647
But that stuff at my house was just to make my father mad .

621
00:46:53,856 --> 00:46:57,401
- But , Ruth- - - l 'm sorry , Dud , but you gotta get real .

622
00:47:06,451 --> 00:47:07,995
Get out of here , gimp !

623
00:47:13,625 --> 00:47:16,170
You 're not my best friend , Mike .

624
00:47:21,758 --> 00:47:23,552
Not anymore .

625
00:47:28,140 --> 00:47:29,892
Dump 's closed , mister .

626
00:47:31,435 --> 00:47:33,729
I 'm just watching the fires .

627
00:47:39,693 --> 00:47:41,195
It scares the animals away .

628
00:47:41,737 --> 00:47:43,280
Just the rats .

629
00:47:43,447 --> 00:47:44,990
Smokes them from their holes .

630
00:47:46,116 --> 00:47:48,243
Yeah . Where will they go ?

631
00:47:48,994 --> 00:47:52,164
I guess they 'll find another hole .

632
00:47:52,331 --> 00:47:53,665
You from around here ?

633
00:47:54,917 --> 00:47:57,294
Yeah , just over the hill .

634
00:47:58,337 --> 00:48:02,090
- What are you writing there ? - Nothing .

635
00:48:03,717 --> 00:48:05,177
I lost my job .

636
00:48:05,344 --> 00:48:08,764
Mike was my best friend since junior high .

637
00:48:08,931 --> 00:48:10,307
It 's his backhoe .

638
00:48:10,474 --> 00:48:13,060
- l 'll wash it off . - No , leave it .

639
00:48:14,895 --> 00:48:17,523
I didn 't do anything wrong .

640
00:48:17,689 --> 00:48:20,943
I was just talking with Ruth Crockett , my girlfriend

641
00:48:21,151 --> 00:48:23,111
and her father got crazy

642
00:48:23,278 --> 00:48:26,865
and told Mike he had to fire me or he 'd lose all his work .

643
00:48:27,032 --> 00:48:29,076
Yeah , that 's too bad .

644
00:48:30,577 --> 00:48:34,581
Say , aren 't you one of the fellas that bought the Marsten place ?

645
00:48:34,748 --> 00:48:39,336
- Very good . - Are there any ghosts in that old house ?

646
00:48:39,503 --> 00:48:40,796
Ghosts ?

647
00:48:42,339 --> 00:48:43,757
No .

648
00:48:43,924 --> 00:48:46,134
- No ghosts . - l didn 't think so .

649
00:48:47,678 --> 00:48:49,263
Well , anyway

650
00:48:49,429 --> 00:48:53,767
it 's always nice when someone comes down to , you know , shoot the breeze

651
00:48:53,976 --> 00:48:57,604
but the dump closes at 6 and it 's half past 9 now , so ... .

652
00:48:57,771 --> 00:48:58,981
Dud

653
00:48:59,523 --> 00:49:01,233
I noticed your limping .

654
00:49:01,733 --> 00:49:03,986
Curvature of the spine ?

655
00:49:05,028 --> 00:49:06,989
- Does that bother you ? - Nope .

656
00:49:07,155 --> 00:49:08,407
I can work fine .

657
00:49:09,241 --> 00:49:11,577
I meant in other ways .

658
00:49:12,744 --> 00:49:14,288
No .

659
00:49:16,206 --> 00:49:17,457
Well

660
00:49:19,001 --> 00:49:20,335
girls .

661
00:49:20,919 --> 00:49:22,671
Just girls .

662
00:49:24,464 --> 00:49:27,259
Their boyfriends , the other kids ?

663
00:49:27,426 --> 00:49:30,679
Sometimes they laugh .

664
00:49:30,846 --> 00:49:34,892
What were you to say if I gave you a chance

665
00:49:35,058 --> 00:49:37,394
to be equal to those boys and girls ?

666
00:49:37,895 --> 00:49:41,523
Or maybe even a little more . Would you take it ?

667
00:49:43,442 --> 00:49:44,693
Equal ?

668
00:49:57,414 --> 00:49:59,249
Danny .

669
00:49:59,958 --> 00:50:01,710
Danny .

670
00:50:03,086 --> 00:50:04,338
Danny .

671
00:50:04,505 --> 00:50:05,589
Danny .

672
00:50:06,256 --> 00:50:08,425
Danny .

673
00:50:08,592 --> 00:50:10,135
Danny ?

674
00:50:10,302 --> 00:50:12,846
Come on , Danny , it 's me

675
00:50:13,055 --> 00:50:14,598
your brother , Ralphie .

676
00:50:15,098 --> 00:50:16,683
Remember ?

677
00:50:16,850 --> 00:50:18,560
You left me in the woods .

678
00:50:18,769 --> 00:50:20,687
Ralphie ?

679
00:50:25,442 --> 00:50:29,613
- l 'm just messing with you , Danny . - Go away .

680
00:50:30,113 --> 00:50:33,325
Danny , I 'm not mad .

681
00:50:33,492 --> 00:50:34,785
Danny .

682
00:50:34,952 --> 00:50:36,370
I knew you were scared .

683
00:50:36,537 --> 00:50:38,956
Cripes , I was scared too .

684
00:50:44,962 --> 00:50:46,672
But not anymore .

685
00:50:48,674 --> 00:50:49,967
Danny

686
00:50:50,133 --> 00:50:51,927
I 'm messing with you , Danny .

687
00:50:56,139 --> 00:50:57,933
I ain 't scared at all .

688
00:50:59,810 --> 00:51:01,061
Let me in , Danny .

689
00:51:01,228 --> 00:51:03,438
Don 't let Mom and Dad blame you .

690
00:51:03,647 --> 00:51:05,941
Let me in , Danny .

691
00:51:07,943 --> 00:51:09,236
All right .

692
00:51:12,197 --> 00:51:14,950
You went to lunch with Sandy McDougall ?

693
00:51:15,117 --> 00:51:17,077
- What 's wrong with that ? - Oh , nothing .

694
00:51:17,244 --> 00:51:22,207
She 's 1 9 , married , barely educated . What else is right ?

695
00:51:22,374 --> 00:51:24,293
What 's going on here ?

696
00:51:40,851 --> 00:51:44,396
Now , who remembers the Morris chair ?

697
00:51:44,563 --> 00:51:45,814
This .

698
00:51:45,981 --> 00:51:48,817
Such an excellent example .

699
00:51:48,984 --> 00:51:51,236
Very popular in Berkeley .

700
00:51:51,403 --> 00:51:53,864
Look at that leather .

701
00:51:54,031 --> 00:51:57,534
Please be kind enough to tell your friends we 're open

702
00:51:57,701 --> 00:52:00,996
and that our prices are so very reasonable .

703
00:52:04,208 --> 00:52:06,043
Madam

704
00:52:06,210 --> 00:52:09,505
this drop-leaf table would look beautiful in a foyer

705
00:52:10,088 --> 00:52:12,549
or in a servants ' entrance .

706
00:52:12,716 --> 00:52:15,802
I am the only servant in my house .

707
00:52:15,969 --> 00:52:18,972
And I am Richard Straker .

708
00:52:20,599 --> 00:52:23,977
Eva Prunier. I own a boarding house on Clift Street .

709
00:52:24,144 --> 00:52:26,396
Eva Prunier .

710
00:52:26,563 --> 00:52:28,857
Your name is familiar .

711
00:52:29,358 --> 00:52:31,151
And your accent .

712
00:52:38,408 --> 00:52:39,576
Excuse me ?

713
00:52:43,789 --> 00:52:45,040
Tell me , Eva

714
00:52:45,207 --> 00:52:48,836
of all the old parlor games , which one do you miss the most ?

715
00:52:49,002 --> 00:52:53,549
As you may share a little morphine avec his little friend .

716
00:52:56,343 --> 00:52:58,095
I am jealous .

717
00:52:58,262 --> 00:53:02,391
You must have been so young at that time then .

718
00:53:02,558 --> 00:53:06,603
All you little village girls , what , 1 6 years old ? Fifteen ?

719
00:53:06,937 --> 00:53:09,022
Did you give to Hubie

720
00:53:09,231 --> 00:53:11,316
what I think you gave to him ?

721
00:53:11,775 --> 00:53:13,068
Oh , I knew it .

722
00:53:13,277 --> 00:53:17,489
- And did you wear his goat 's-head mask ? - Stop it !

723
00:53:21,910 --> 00:53:24,705
I taught Ben Mears in the eighth grade . He survived .

724
00:53:26,748 --> 00:53:30,544
Since then , he 's had a distinguished literary career .

725
00:53:30,711 --> 00:53:33,714
In 2001 , he was captured by Taliban troops

726
00:53:33,922 --> 00:53:36,091
while reporting the Afghan war .

727
00:53:36,300 --> 00:53:39,636
He was rescued from certain death by U.S. Marines .

728
00:53:39,970 --> 00:53:41,555
On the return trek

729
00:53:41,763 --> 00:53:44,224
Ben 's Marines killed 1 0 Afghan villagers .

730
00:53:44,391 --> 00:53:48,145
Damage Control is a factual account of the incident .

731
00:53:48,312 --> 00:53:51,607
Three Marines were court-martialed and imprisoned .

732
00:53:52,566 --> 00:53:56,987
Ben received the Pulitzer Prize . Mr. Mears is in town researching his new book

733
00:53:57,863 --> 00:53:59,489
on the Marsten house .

734
00:54:00,449 --> 00:54:04,203
Mr. Mears , should anyone in their right mind trust an author ?

735
00:54:04,828 --> 00:54:06,997
A good author illuminates truth .

736
00:54:08,332 --> 00:54:11,627
- Yes . - What 's the truth about this town ?

737
00:54:12,252 --> 00:54:14,796
I used to think nothing happened here .

738
00:54:15,005 --> 00:54:17,549
But the truth is everything happens here .

739
00:54:17,716 --> 00:54:20,302
One has to look close in a small town .

740
00:54:20,511 --> 00:54:22,471
The beauty is in the details .

741
00:54:22,679 --> 00:54:28,185
You have all the horror of Qalai Janghi prison right here in one battered child .

742
00:54:28,352 --> 00:54:32,814
All the beauty of Michelangelo in the alabaster calf of one

743
00:54:32,981 --> 00:54:34,942
shoulder-high waitress .

744
00:54:35,108 --> 00:54:38,403
The longing you feel for the boy or girl in the next row

745
00:54:38,570 --> 00:54:42,074
is equal to or greater than what your favorite musician feels

746
00:54:42,241 --> 00:54:44,201
for his favorite supermodel .

747
00:54:45,118 --> 00:54:47,204
Never minimize your feelings .

748
00:54:48,914 --> 00:54:50,332
Or this town .

749
00:54:52,167 --> 00:54:55,629
What 's the truth about the Marines that saved you in Afghanistan ?

750
00:54:59,550 --> 00:55:01,635
I 'm not a waitress or shoulder-high .

751
00:55:02,177 --> 00:55:05,931
- Let me checked those Michelangelo calves . - lt was metaphors on the fly .

752
00:55:06,098 --> 00:55:08,350
- What do you want from me ? - Proof .

753
00:55:08,559 --> 00:55:10,185
And they really liked him ?

754
00:55:10,394 --> 00:55:12,729
I 'll say they warmed up to him .

755
00:55:14,106 --> 00:55:17,568
The boy went from mental shock to extreme anemia overnight .

756
00:55:17,985 --> 00:55:20,362
What our grandfathers would call wasting away .

757
00:55:20,571 --> 00:55:22,322
That poor family . Two sons .

758
00:55:22,489 --> 00:55:23,907
Can you imagine ?

759
00:55:24,074 --> 00:55:29,788
The red-cell count on a 1 4-year-old boy should run between 85 and 95 percent .

760
00:55:29,955 --> 00:55:31,248
Danny 's was 45 .

