1490
01:52:15,027 --> 01:52:17,154
Well , of course . Thank you .

1491
01:52:17,321 --> 01:52:19,072
It 's a tragedy .

1492
01:53:8,288 --> 01:53:10,249
- Norton 's Cafe . - Hi .

1493
01:53:10,457 --> 01:53:12,793
- ls Susan there ? - Susan 's left work , Ben .

1494
01:53:13,001 --> 01:53:14,795
Did she say where she was going ?

1495
01:53:14,962 --> 01:53:17,047
No . She got a little upset ...

1496
01:53:17,214 --> 01:53:20,467
- ... when she heard about Floyd . - Does she have a cell phone ?

1497
01:53:20,634 --> 01:53:23,845
- l 'm afraid not . - Thank you .

1498
01:53:26,306 --> 01:53:27,933
- lt 's all right . - Who are you ?

1499
01:53:28,100 --> 01:53:32,563
I 'm Mark Petrie. I know you . You 're Sue Norton . My mother knows your father .

1500
01:53:32,854 --> 01:53:36,024
Joyce Petrie. lt 's my mother . The waitress at Giaco 's .

1501
01:53:36,191 --> 01:53:39,444
- What are you doing here ? - What are you doing here ?

1502
01:53:39,611 --> 01:53:41,822
Did you come to kill the vampires ?

1503
01:53:42,239 --> 01:53:47,286
- A friend died last night . - One of them tried to get me .

1504
01:53:48,328 --> 01:53:51,874
That was Richard Straker in the SUV . He 's moving around by day

1505
01:53:52,040 --> 01:53:54,251
so he must be the watchdog .

1506
01:53:54,418 --> 01:53:59,131
The vampire 's name is Barlow . And he 's the partner that nobody 's seen yet .

1507
01:53:59,298 --> 01:54:1,884
You 're not the only one talking about vampires .

1508
01:54:2,050 --> 01:54:4,761
- Who else ? - A teacher and a doctor .

1509
01:54:7,806 --> 01:54:11,685
- You okay ? - lt 's that house .

1510
01:54:12,686 --> 01:54:16,815
A writer friend of mine spent a horrific night there when he was a kid .

1511
01:54:16,982 --> 01:54:19,109
- Ben Mears ? - You know him ?

1512
01:54:19,276 --> 01:54:23,071
I know the story . Did you bring a stake too ?

1513
01:54:25,616 --> 01:54:29,912
Yeah . That 's cool , but I don 't think it 's going to work .

1514
01:54:30,078 --> 01:54:31,872
Don 't believe everything you read .

1515
01:54:43,175 --> 01:54:45,135
Come in .

1516
01:54:45,302 --> 01:54:50,224
- Hello , Father . - Ed , come in . Have a seat .

1517
01:54:50,390 --> 01:54:53,518
We have something to celebrate today , Father .

1518
01:54:53,685 --> 01:54:57,439
- What would that be ? - Eva Prunier has agreed to marry me .

1519
01:54:57,606 --> 01:55:0,692
- Well , congratulations . - Persistence and patience .

1520
01:55:0,901 --> 01:55:3,695
And love . Nothing good ever happens without love .

1521
01:55:3,862 --> 01:55:7,824
We 'd like to do it tomorrow . A small ceremony . Very simple .

1522
01:55:7,991 --> 01:55:11,328
- That is , if you 're available . - lt would be an honor .

1523
01:55:11,495 --> 01:55:13,664
I 've had some good news meself .

1524
01:55:13,830 --> 01:55:16,917
Unusual , but good . A true battle .

1525
01:55:17,125 --> 01:55:21,296
Perhaps there 's a need for this religious relic after all . Care for a Jameson 's ?

1526
01:55:21,463 --> 01:55:23,423
Never say no .

1527
01:55:24,132 --> 01:55:26,718
Here 's to your marriage and the death of Freud .

1528
01:55:26,885 --> 01:55:31,306
- Slainte . - Father , maybe I 'll wait on this drink ...

1529
01:55:31,473 --> 01:55:35,686
- ... what with the wedding tomorrow and all . - No . Has she 's reformed you already ?

1530
01:55:37,896 --> 01:55:41,191
Perhaps I 'll abstain as well .

1531
01:55:49,700 --> 01:55:51,410
Closed .

1532
01:55:51,577 --> 01:55:53,161
Closed all day .

1533
01:55:54,037 --> 01:55:55,414
Thank you .

1534
01:56:23,650 --> 01:56:26,320
Stop . We 'll call the police .

1535
01:56:26,486 --> 01:56:28,447
- l have friends who can help . - No .

1536
01:56:28,614 --> 01:56:31,658
I 'm going in before that kid comes back to my window .

1537
01:56:32,159 --> 01:56:35,245
- l 'll go . You keep watch . - No , thanks .

1538
01:56:55,599 --> 01:57:0,020
When we find him , don 't look into his eyes , okay ?

1539
01:57:0,187 --> 01:57:4,441
He sleeps in a coffin until dark , but he can still hook you with his eyes .

1540
01:57:4,608 --> 01:57:8,445
Do you hear what you 're saying ? Do you really believe this ?

1541
01:57:8,612 --> 01:57:12,157
What if Barlow is just an ordinary serial killer ?

1542
01:57:12,324 --> 01:57:13,951
You wish .

1543
01:57:17,079 --> 01:57:19,665
- Oh , God , do you smell that ? - Yes .

1544
01:57:19,873 --> 01:57:22,709
- lt 's worse in here , isn 't it ? - Yes .

1545
01:57:27,130 --> 01:57:29,341
That 's where we have to go .

1546
01:57:35,305 --> 01:57:38,850
- l can hear my heart . - l can hear your heart too .

1547
01:57:39,560 --> 01:57:42,020
Mark . Oh , no .

1548
01:57:47,150 --> 01:57:50,988
The police are on their way . That was an alarm you triggered .

1549
01:57:51,154 --> 01:57:53,657
- We-- - Don 't come any closer .

1550
01:57:53,824 --> 01:57:56,743
Just take whatever it is you have and leave .

1551
01:57:56,910 --> 01:58:0,831
- We 're not stealing anything . We 're just- - - What do you want ?

1552
01:58:1,206 --> 01:58:4,918
- Are there more of you ? - No . Look , I 'm sorry .

1553
01:58:5,127 --> 01:58:6,795
We were curious about the house .

1554
01:58:6,962 --> 01:58:10,090
We heard it was sold , but we didn 't think anyone lived here .

1555
01:58:13,051 --> 01:58:14,553
You 're trespassing .

1556
01:58:16,930 --> 01:58:19,391
What does he have there ? You 're armed .

1557
01:58:20,767 --> 01:58:23,228
- lt 's just a hammer and some wood . - A hammer ?

1558
01:58:23,729 --> 01:58:25,397
You 've come to vandalize ?

1559
01:58:25,564 --> 01:58:29,776
No , look , I 'm Susan Norton . I 've lived in Salem 's Lot my whole life .

1560
01:58:29,943 --> 01:58:33,614
This is Mark Petrie . We know you just moved here , and- -

1561
01:58:33,780 --> 01:58:39,244
And this is the way you welcome me ? With hammers and guns ?

1562
01:58:42,289 --> 01:58:44,666
You

1563
01:58:44,833 --> 01:58:46,376
show me that .

1564
01:58:51,965 --> 01:58:54,009
What is this ?

1565
01:58:54,968 --> 01:58:57,804
is this a weapon ? is it ?

1566
01:58:57,971 --> 01:58:59,223
- No . - ls it ?

1567
01:59:0,349 --> 01:59:1,600
No !

1568
01:59:2,809 --> 01:59:4,978
Fine !

1569
01:59:10,651 --> 01:59:14,696
- Help ! Help ! - Go on !

1570
01:59:22,204 --> 01:59:25,415
- Help ! - Three .

1571
01:59:35,551 --> 01:59:37,636
Two .

1572
01:59:42,015 --> 01:59:43,517
Help !

1573
01:59:46,979 --> 01:59:50,023
One . Time 's up .

1574
02:00:4,454 --> 02:00:6,456
Oh , this is ridiculous .

1575
02:00:8,584 --> 02:00:10,419
I 'm killing my career .

1576
02:00:13,213 --> 02:00:15,132
I 'm being blackmailed .

1577
02:00:15,299 --> 02:00:16,800
Professionally ?

1578
02:00:16,967 --> 02:00:19,136
It was very unprofessional on my part .

1579
02:00:19,303 --> 02:00:24,224
If you saw the man 's wife , you might think it was understandable

1580
02:00:24,433 --> 02:00:27,936
but certainly not professional or forgivable .

1581
02:00:28,729 --> 02:00:31,356
I 'm surprised . I didn 't think doctors had penises .

1582
02:00:32,816 --> 02:00:34,693
Yeah , it 's an industry secret .

1583
02:00:34,860 --> 02:00:39,072
We usually try to keep it between ourselves and the nurses .

1584
02:00:39,239 --> 02:00:41,074
How much ?

1585
02:00:41,241 --> 02:00:44,286
Ten thousand , by today .

1586
02:00:45,704 --> 02:00:48,415
He threatened to call the board earlier .

1587
02:00:48,582 --> 02:00:51,168
I might not even be a doctor right now .

1588
02:00:51,418 --> 02:00:55,380
You 're too busy to be a doctor . You 're a vampire hunter .

1589
02:00:56,089 --> 02:00:59,426
- We should be home by midnight . - That would be Cinderella .

1590
02:01:7,851 --> 02:01:11,104
I can 't stay any longer. lt 's useless . I gotta go find Susan .

1591
02:01:11,271 --> 02:01:13,106
What if she went up to the house ?

1592
02:01:18,570 --> 02:01:20,155
Oh , my God .

1593
02:01:23,242 --> 02:01:24,701
Ralphie ?

1594
02:01:26,161 --> 02:01:27,955
Where are you , sweetheart ?

1595
02:01:30,123 --> 02:01:32,584
Marge ? You okay ?

1596
02:01:47,641 --> 02:01:49,351
Use the cross !

1597
02:01:55,691 --> 02:01:56,984
She bit me !

1598
02:02:13,500 --> 02:02:15,752
She bit me ! She bit me !

1599
02:02:15,919 --> 02:02:17,671
She bit me !

1600
02:02:17,838 --> 02:02:19,798
Give me my bag ! Give me my bag !

1601
02:02:22,467 --> 02:02:23,886
She bit me .

1602
02:02:28,307 --> 02:02:30,017
Tetanus .

1603
02:02:34,730 --> 02:02:36,481
In my heart .

1604
02:02:36,857 --> 02:02:38,609
Do it ! Hurry up !

1605
02:02:45,449 --> 02:02:46,867
Did we get it ?

1606
02:02:47,034 --> 02:02:48,911
You should call me in the morning .

1607
02:03:17,773 --> 02:03:19,399
Hello ?

1608
02:03:42,422 --> 02:03:43,840
Susan !

1609
02:03:48,470 --> 02:03:52,641
Ben , there 's no car . Would she really come up here by herself ?

1610
02:03:58,021 --> 02:04:1,066
If you think so , we 'll go in . If not , we should find her .

1611
02:04:1,233 --> 02:04:3,360
We 'll come back together with a plan .

1612
02:04:12,452 --> 02:04:15,789
You wanna be a Bloody Pirate , don 't you ? Go on , Mears .

1613
02:04:16,164 --> 02:04:19,418
- Unless he kills you . - if Hubie kills you , you 're in !

1614
02:04:24,965 --> 02:04:26,800
Susan !

1615
02:04:27,968 --> 02:04:29,177
Ben , come on .

1616
02:04:29,928 --> 02:04:32,973
Call Norton 's . Let 's check her house .

1617
02:05:2,419 --> 02:05:4,171
Help ! Help me , please !

1618
02:05:5,172 --> 02:05:9,134
- Help ! - Here I come , ready or not .

1619
02:05:16,516 --> 02:05:18,185
Where are you ?

1620
02:05:34,159 --> 02:05:36,537
- Susan ! - Mark ?

1621
02:05:36,703 --> 02:05:39,081
I can 't see. lt 's so dark .

1622
02:05:42,292 --> 02:05:45,796
- Come down , boy . - l know your name !

1623
02:05:45,963 --> 02:05:50,384
- l admire you . Come down for a taste . - lt 's Barlow !

1624
02:05:50,551 --> 02:05:55,180
There 's enough here for two . Why would you run , boy ?

1625
02:06:2,729 --> 02:06:4,398
Susan !

1626
02:06:9,069 --> 02:06:10,612
Susan !

1627
02:06:23,208 --> 02:06:27,212
i 'd like to drop everything and help , Ben , but i have four missing people

1628
02:06:27,379 --> 02:06:29,172
and three dead .

1629
02:06:29,715 --> 02:06:32,718
When was the last time you heard from Susan ?

1630
02:06:34,011 --> 02:06:37,180
- lt was about nine hours ago . - That 's not so long .

1631
02:06:37,347 --> 02:06:42,019
I 've been to her house , the cafe , the gym , the library . Nobody knows where she is .

1632
02:06:42,185 --> 02:06:46,440
What 's going on , Mr. Mears ? Do you know ? Because i don 't .

1633
02:06:46,607 --> 02:06:50,360
i have suspicions , but if i don 't know , i can 't help .

1634
02:06:53,155 --> 02:06:54,823
You wouldn 't believe me .

1635
02:06:55,449 --> 02:06:57,326
Ben ?

1636
02:06:59,453 --> 02:07:1,288
Be careful , Parkins .

1637
02:07:5,375 --> 02:07:6,752
Susan ?

1638
02:07:37,824 --> 02:07:42,037
Closed. lt was closed yesterday too .

1639
02:07:42,246 --> 02:07:43,747
Thanks .

1640
02:07:46,750 --> 02:07:48,502
Thank you kindly .

1641
02:07:51,630 --> 02:07:53,674
Ed , breakfast is ready .

1642
02:08:22,744 --> 02:08:24,162
Ed ?

1643
02:08:27,249 --> 02:08:28,500
Yeah ?

1644
02:08:29,376 --> 02:08:31,503
is there a writer here named Ben ?

1645
02:08:31,670 --> 02:08:33,881
- Ben Mears . - Yeah , could you get him ?

1646
02:08:34,047 --> 02:08:37,009
- Please ? - He may be sleeping .

1647
02:08:37,175 --> 02:08:40,345
No , he 'd want you to wake him up . Please .

1648
02:09:9,041 --> 02:09:10,417
Morning .

1649
02:09:10,584 --> 02:09:13,670
- Are you the friend of Sue Norton ? - Yes . Have you seen her ?

1650
02:09:13,837 --> 02:09:15,172
Ben .

1651
02:09:15,547 --> 02:09:19,176
- Ben , have you seen Ed this morning ? - No , I haven 't .

1652
02:09:19,343 --> 02:09:22,304
- We 're getting married today . - Married ?

1653
02:09:22,471 --> 02:09:24,681
- Can I talk to you outside ? - Of course .

1654
02:09:24,848 --> 02:09:26,683
Congratulations .

1655
02:09:39,446 --> 02:09:41,740
We went in the house through that window .

1656
02:09:42,241 --> 02:09:45,994
She 's still up there ! Right now . Look , I don 't know what she ... .

1657
02:09:52,834 --> 02:09:56,004
l 'm with Mark Petrie . He was with her . I 'm headed there now .

1658
02:09:56,171 --> 02:09:58,465
You can 't barge in. i can get a warrant ...

1659
02:09:58,632 --> 02:10:0,092
- ... within the hour . - Stop .

1660
02:10:0,300 --> 02:10:2,344
I gotta go , chief. I 'll call you back .

1661
02:10:19,987 --> 02:10:24,241
Father , with what Mark says and Susan 's car , that 's proof enough for me .

1662
02:10:24,408 --> 02:10:27,244
Hold on a minute . What if Straker 's partner is armed ?

1663
02:10:27,411 --> 02:10:29,496
How are you gonna protect yourself ?

1664
02:10:30,747 --> 02:10:32,958
I made these up last night .

1665
02:10:33,333 --> 02:10:35,168
- Take that . - Son , stay in the car .

1666
02:10:35,335 --> 02:10:36,795
I 'm going .

1667
02:10:37,004 --> 02:10:42,259
- Maybe you 'd rather stay behind , Father . - No , I 'll go . This team needs a clear head .

1668
02:10:43,719 --> 02:10:47,014
Vampires . Would have been a lot easier to accept

1669
02:10:47,180 --> 02:10:51,310
if you could have arranged for a thunderstorm or a power failure .

1670
02:10:51,685 --> 02:10:54,771
Would a dancing Marjorie Glick do it for you ?

1671
02:11:2,863 --> 02:11:4,406
It 's a loan .

1672
02:11:5,282 --> 02:11:7,492
Ten thousand ? I can 't take this from you .

1673
02:11:7,951 --> 02:11:10,996
When this is over , we 're gonna need your good reputation .

1674
02:11:11,872 --> 02:11:15,918
- Thanks , man . - You guys hear about the hippie vampire ?

1675
02:11:17,127 --> 02:11:20,839
He 's ghoul , man . Real ghoul .

1676
02:11:24,259 --> 02:11:27,971
- You 're doing well , Ben . - Oh , yeah ? How so ?

1677
02:11:28,138 --> 02:11:32,059
Only a trained physician can see that you 're scared out of your mind .

1678
02:11:36,313 --> 02:11:40,442
I 've never been up here before , at least not this close .

1679
02:11:46,573 --> 02:11:48,200
Hold on .

1680
02:11:48,367 --> 02:11:50,369
Let cooler heads prevail .

1681
02:11:54,331 --> 02:11:55,749
Hello ?

1682
02:11:57,334 --> 02:11:59,169
- Hello ? - Susan !

1683
02:11:59,336 --> 02:12:0,921
Hello !

1684
02:12:2,172 --> 02:12:4,216
Straker 's upstairs .

1685
02:12:5,551 --> 02:12:7,135
There 's something different .

1686
02:13:21,919 --> 02:13:25,631
- He 's bled dry . - Holy Mother of God .

1687
02:13:25,797 --> 02:13:27,132
I didn 't do that .

1688
02:13:32,262 --> 02:13:36,558
I tried to go down , but I didn 't .

1689
02:13:54,368 --> 02:13:56,203
I know what 's different .

1690
02:13:57,246 --> 02:13:59,164
It doesn 't smell anymore .

1691
02:14:0,123 --> 02:14:1,667
Over here .

1692
02:14:34,157 --> 02:14:35,993
Give me the stake .

1693
02:14:38,370 --> 02:14:41,790
Hold on . You have to make sure .

1694
02:14:42,374 --> 02:14:46,169
If he 's dead , you 're only desecrating a corpse . But if he 's not ... .

1695
02:14:51,425 --> 02:14:53,051
Legally dead .

1696
02:15:29,004 --> 02:15:30,923
Saints preserve us .

1697
02:15:47,773 --> 02:15:49,274
Here !

1698
02:16:16,802 --> 02:16:19,680
My God . What monster did this ?

1699
02:16:28,689 --> 02:16:29,940
She 's dead .

1700
02:16:30,774 --> 02:16:32,276
Or undead .

1701
02:16:33,402 --> 02:16:35,487
Wait ! Wait !

1702
02:16:39,199 --> 02:16:42,160
What if we kill Barlow and they all come back to life ?

1703
02:16:42,828 --> 02:16:44,329
Or they just die .

1704
02:16:44,496 --> 02:16:46,832
- You don 't really believe that . - But what if ?

1705
02:16:46,999 --> 02:16:51,211
Please , not Susan . We know where she is .

1706
02:16:51,378 --> 02:16:53,297
We can come back if we have to .

1707
02:16:53,463 --> 02:16:56,216
- What if she infects someone else ? - Please .

1708
02:16:56,383 --> 02:16:57,801
Please .

1709
02:17:0,220 --> 02:17:1,930
It 's been a gruesome day .

1710
02:17:5,976 --> 02:17:8,312
Rest in peace .

1711
02:17:24,244 --> 02:17:29,208
- Who 's poking around the Marsten house ? - Can 't say from this distance .

1712
02:17:31,043 --> 02:17:33,295
Town looks a little dead today .

1713
02:17:33,837 --> 02:17:36,256
Maybe I 'll take a ride up and see .

1714
02:17:36,590 --> 02:17:39,593
They 're leaving , Nolly . Let it be .

1715
02:17:39,760 --> 02:17:42,262
Sometimes these badges get in the way .

1716
02:17:42,429 --> 02:17:45,474
Our badges ? What do you mean ?

1717
02:17:46,433 --> 02:17:50,062
- Are you all right , Parkins ? - No .

1718
02:17:50,729 --> 02:17:52,773
I 'm scared .

1719
02:17:59,530 --> 02:18:3,575
On lighter occasions , these used to hold the perfect martini .

1720
02:18:3,784 --> 02:18:7,246
There 's a presence in that house . I don 't know if you can feel it .

1721
02:18:7,412 --> 02:18:9,122
Oh , I can feel it .

1722
02:18:9,289 --> 02:18:12,167
I felt it before , when I was a boy and I went inside .

1723
02:18:12,334 --> 02:18:14,711
I thought it was me. I thought it was

1724
02:18:14,878 --> 02:18:18,131
some manifestation of my own fear .

1725
02:18:18,590 --> 02:18:20,592
It wasn 't .

1726
02:18:22,803 --> 02:18:26,139
- What is it ? - The unholy spirit .

1727
02:18:26,807 --> 02:18:29,226
Dull , mindless , moronic evil .

1728
02:18:29,393 --> 02:18:32,604
As familiar in the confessional as the smell of old velvet .

1729
02:18:32,771 --> 02:18:37,276
Marsten invited the unholy spirit into his house and home , and there it resides .

1730
02:18:38,068 --> 02:18:42,197
In that house , it feels so familiar . It feels like it 's coming from inside me .

1731
02:18:43,991 --> 02:18:46,243
Evil comes from inside of all of us .

1732
02:18:50,497 --> 02:18:54,251
I 've made a fine career turning the hard mirror on other people .

1733
02:18:54,668 --> 02:18:57,421
Would you feel more comfortable in the confessional ?

1734
02:18:57,588 --> 02:19:0,799
